# Domain Entities

Entities map 1-to-1 to database tables. Keep them anemic; business logic lives in Actions and Domain Services.

## Rules

- Inherit `BaseEntity` — you automatically get `Id`, `CreatedAt`, `UpdatedAt`, `DeletedAt`, `IsDeleted`, `IAuditable`, `ISoftDeletable`.
- Properties only (plus navigation collections). No methods except trivial computed read-only helpers that touch only this entity's own fields.
- No references to `LoadlyAggregator.API`, `LoadlyAggregator.Infrastructure`, FluentValidation, EF attributes, or JSON attributes. Column names/relations live in EF `Configurations/`.
- Give collections a safe default: `= new List<Address>();`.
- Enums are stored as their underlying int via the entity configuration; keep the property as the enum type.
- Keep foreign-key id properties (`CompanyId`) **and** a navigation property only when a relationship is actively used in queries.

## Example

```csharp
public class Admin : BaseEntity, IAuthenticatable
{
    public string FullName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string UserName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Email { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Phone { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Password { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public AdminType Type { get; set; }
    public UserStatus Status { get; set; }
    public CommunicationChannel MfaChannel { get; set; }

    public ICollection<UserRole> UserRoles { get; set; } = new List<UserRole>();
    public ICollection<Address> Addresses { get; set; } = new List<Address>();
}
```

## Soft delete

- Never add a bool `IsDeleted` column — the base class exposes `IsDeleted => DeletedAt != null`.
- Hard-deletes are not allowed via the repository; use `Remove()` which sets `DeletedAt`.
- Query results exclude soft-deleted rows automatically; pass `includeDeleted: true` only when explicitly needed.
